From 4186b232de38c0f8f83c4198883c1327ac3f3540 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Roessner <c@roessner.co>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 12:39:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] bounce: expose trusted origin evidence to Milters at EOH

Capture the exact envelope sender and recipient records while bounce(8)
already scans the original queue file. Treat a DONE record as the in-place
replacement of an original RCPT record, and exclude canceled recipients.
Encode a bounded, versioned binary record as unpadded base64url.

Use the private dsn_cleanup path for the null-sender notifications produced
by bounce_notify_service(), bounce_warn_service(), bounce_one_service(),
and bounce_notify_verp(). If complete evidence is unavailable, retain the
existing best-effort public cleanup path and do not assert provenance.

Expose the provenance marker, original queue ID, and original envelope only
as requested end-of-header Milter macros. They are absent at all earlier
events and for messages that did not arrive through the private handoff.
Action and status remain in the RFC 3464 delivery-status part and are not
duplicated in macro values.

Use the EOH macro class because milter8_message() supplies eod_macros with
BODY chunks as well as SMFIC_BODYEOB. EOH is the standard once-per-message
stage immediately before the DSN body; the filter retains the provenance and
does not act until EOM.

The Milter wire protocol is unchanged. Filters opt in through normal macro
negotiation, and filters that do not request the new names are unaffected.

Tested with:

    make -j4
    make -C src/milter tests
    make -C src/cleanup test_cleanup_envelope

The bounce test vector validates the exact unpadded base64url value. The
stock bounce reference-test wrapper needs non-conflicting Postfix service
accounts and therefore cannot run unchanged on macOS installations that
provide both postfix/_postfix and postdrop/_postdrop aliases.
